indi-scopelink (1.4) jammy; urgency=medium

  * Every motor's position in its own steps, and whether it is turning clockwise, counterclockwise or
    not at all, beside its load on the Telemetry tab (MOTOR_POSITION, MOTOR_MOTION). A move made from
    the Calibration tab shows there too.
  * The front flap can be stopped where it is (FLAP_ABORT), which INDI's dust cap interface has no
    control for.
  * Each stored fault as one line of JSON with its whole freeze frame (FAULT_DETAILS), which the log
    cuts short, and one fault can be cleared without the rest (FAULT_CLEAR).
  * The controller's own supplies, temperature, load and bus errors are always on the Telemetry tab;
    the Controller diagnostics option that hid them is gone.
  * Read fault store and Clear fault store work again on firmware from August 2026 on, which answers a
    request without its routine id with nothing: any stored fault made both fail with "No valid
    response to command 0x05".
  * The simulator stores a second fault, and clears one fault or all of them as the firmware does. It
    also answers a fault store read without the routine id with nothing, as the firmware does.

 -- Bence Toth <bence.toth@astrolabs.hu>  Sat, 28 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0100

indi-scopelink (1.3) jammy; urgency=medium

  * Interface version 1.3 is supported: either auxiliary power output can run as a dew heater, set by
    hand or under the controller's automatic dew control, with a lamp saying whether it is following
    the dew point.
  * The power outputs can be named, in the driver's configuration, and every control of an output
    carries its name.
  * Switching one auxiliary output no longer sends the other one its state as well, which on a dew
    heater under automatic control would have taken it off automatic.
  * A dew heater duty outside 0 to 100 % is refused, rather than clamped to full power.
  * Restart controller could reconnect to the controller before it had reset, which acknowledges the
    request and resets about a second later, and then lose it again halfway through reading the motor
    assignment. A controller now counts as back only once it has left the bus, and it is given a
    minute rather than thirty seconds to return.
  * The udev rule is now 70-scopelink.rules. Numbered 99 it tagged the controller for uaccess after
    systemd's 73-seat-late.rules had already run, so the user at the console was given no access and
    only dialout membership let anybody in.

 -- Bence Toth <bence.toth@astrolabs.hu>  Fri, 20 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0100

indi-scopelink (1.2) jammy; urgency=medium

  * Interface version 1.2 is supported: the controller names its sensor module, and the status
    frame carries humidity, dew point and three axes of acceleration where the module has them.
  * New Climate and Tilt telemetry, smoothed, with the margin above the dew point.
  * New tube orientation, altitude and roll, with an optional level reference kept in the
    driver's configuration.
  * Temperatures are converted with 273.15 rather than 273.
  * The rotator's sync offset is restored from the saved configuration rather than reset to zero.
  * A firmware update reports read protection the way the newer boot loader does.

 -- Bence Toth <bence.toth@astrolabs.hu>  Mon, 26 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0100

indi-scopelink (1.1) jammy; urgency=medium

  * Hardware generation 4 and interface version 1.1 are supported.
  * The controller's motor assignment is read at connect: which motor focuses, which rotates and
    which ones the front flap is made of.
  * New rotator interface, offered on a controller with a motor assigned and calibrated for it.
  * Configuration parameters are generated from the firmware's own description, with its limits,
    its units and its groups. Property names changed with them.
  * The udev rule matches the USB identifiers assigned to Astrolabs, and /dev/scopelink is back.

 -- Bence Toth <bence.toth@astrolabs.hu>  Mon, 07 Sep 2026 21:00:00 +0200

